# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — Root-level ignore rules for the Lundi AI Chatbot monorepo
#
# Purpose: Prevent sensitive, generated, and environment-specific files from
#          being committed to source control.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment variable files
# CRITICAL: .env files contain secrets such as the OPENAI_API_KEY. Committing
# secrets to a repository — even a private one — is a serious security risk.
# Anyone with read access to the repo (including future collaborators or a
# leaked token) could abuse those credentials. Always use .env.example to
# document which variables are required, and keep actual values out of git.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node.js dependencies
# node_modules/ directories are large, OS-specific, and fully reproducible by
# running `npm install`. Committing them bloats the repository and causes
# unnecessary merge conflicts. Consumers install their own copies from
# package.json / package-lock.json.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compiled output — TypeScript / Vite build artifacts
# dist/ and build/ contain the compiled JavaScript output produced by `tsc` or
# the Vite bundler. These files are derived artifacts: they can always be
# regenerated from source and should never be manually edited. Excluding them
# keeps the repository focused on source code and avoids committing files that
# differ across machines or build environments.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
